Algorithm:


Start the program and set root = NULL.
Define a node with data, left, right, lthread and rthread. A new node has both flags true and both pointers NULL.
Read a key to insert. If the tree is empty, make the new node the root.
Otherwise, start at the root and move left if key < data, or right if key > data. Stop when the next link is a thread, and ignore duplicate keys.
If the key is smaller than the parent, set new->left = parent->left and new->right = parent. Then set parent->left = new and parent->lthread = false.
If the key is larger than the parent, set new->right = parent->right and new->left = parent. Then set parent->right = new and parent->rthread = false.
Read the key whose predecessor and successor are required, and search for it by following only real child links.
If the node is not found, display "Node not found" and stop.
For the successor, if rthread = true, the successor is node->right, which may be NULL.
If rthread = false, go to the right child and keep moving left until lthread = true. That node is the successor.
For the predecessor, if lthread = true, the predecessor is node->left, which may be NULL.
If lthread = false, go to the left child and keep moving right until rthread = true. That node is the predecessor.
Display the predecessor and successor, or print "does not exist" where the value is NULL.
Free the allocated memory and stop the program.